 ## Background
-*   **Origin:** The method is based on work by Evans [Eva06a], who suggested influencing the surface point normal to better approximate sky effects [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **History:** It is presented as Algorithm 3.7 in the source material, modifying the earlier Algorithm 3.4 (standard Evans AO) [S1, S2, unofficial]. The changes include adding the normal modification step, changing the accumulation base from 2 to 1.1, and explicitly showing the ray equation [S1, S2, unofficial].
-*   **Usage:** Used in GPU ray marching of distance fields for ambient occlusion, particularly in contexts where visual fidelity for curved surfaces is prioritized over robustness across all geometry types [S1, S2, unofficial].
